# One-dimensional heating of a slab over a sink: the surface follows a series of exponentials whose slowest time constant is 4 d^2 / (pi^2 alpha).
# Reference: the time to 63% from that series, within 3% (implicit Euler steps and a heater one cell thick).
title Step response of a 2 um oxide slab heated over its whole surface
grid dx=0.5 dy=0.0625
window width=4 ymin=-2 ymax=0
heater h xmin=-2 xmax=2 ymin=-0.0625 ymax=0 power=0.1
probe top x=0.25 y=-0.03125
transient heater=h dt=0.008 steps=2500
expect response top h 356.657609 1e-7
expect peak 35.6657609 1e-7
expect balance 1e-9
expect cells 256
expect tau top 1.527048 1e-6
expect rise top 3.9469085 1e-6
expect tau top 1.495 0.03
